        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "**Track:** styles | **Difficulty:** 4/10 | **Time:** ~10 min"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Modes explain tunes that don't behave like textbook major or minor — central to authentic Irish and Scottish harmonisation."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "dorian",
      "title": "Dorian",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Minor 3rd, major 6th. A dorian: A B C D E F♯ G A. 'Banish Misfortune' often analysed as A dorian."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "mixolydian",
      "title": "Mixolydian",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Major 3rd, flat 7th. D mixolydian: D E F♯ G A B C D. Many D-centred tunes use C natural."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "harmonising",
      "title": "Harmonising",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Don't sharp the characteristic flat note. Mode-aware backup keeps sessions sounding authentic."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "entities": [],
  "entity_order": [],
  "playlist": [],
  "tunes": [],
